                                "sense_id": "dcfec39f-7e1d-3ea7-9d47-93032198a471",
                                "text": "[…]high up on an overhanging rock, perhaps twenty feet above the ground, a ghostly white thylacine was clearly visible. Thylacines, or Tasmanian tigers, have been extinct on the mainland of Australia for at least two thousand years."
                            }
                        ]
